WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 10.1 · Legal, Compliance, Policies & Risk
Your legal and regulatory map

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Know the legal duties you will carry, and ask the right questions before you launch.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:27.393
A legal map lists the legal duties you will carry: where each comes from, who oversees it, when it applies and who is responsible. It helps you ask the right questions before you launch.

4
00:00:27.793 --> 00:00:28.393
Four sources of duties

5
00:00:28.393 --> 00:00:40.463
Your legal form: Association, foundation, charity, company or cooperative: each brings its own registration and governance rules. For example: Registering as a company with a social purpose brings annual accounts and filing deadlines.

6
00:00:40.463 --> 00:00:50.681
Your activities: Working with children, employing people, handling data, selling food or raising money. For example: The bakery needs food hygiene registration before its first market stall.

7
00:00:50.681 --> 00:01:02.381
Your countries: Each country and region where you work has its own rules. For example: Our bakery works in one country, so it maps national rules and the city’s market rules.

8
00:01:02.381 --> 00:01:13.800
Funders and partners: Grant and contract conditions can be legally binding. For example: The local youth fund requires insurance and a safeguarding policy before the first trainee starts.

9
00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:14.800
Why map it now

10
00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:21.585
1. Some duties start before you register; others the day you first hire or sell.

11
00:01:21.585 --> 00:01:27.630
2. Knowing your questions saves time with someone who has a legal background.

12
00:01:27.630 --> 00:01:33.563
3. Funders and partners expect you to know your obligations.

13
00:01:33.963 --> 00:01:34.563
What it feeds

14
00:01:34.563 --> 00:01:39.867
1. Your policy needs assessment and policy register in this module.

15
00:01:39.867 --> 00:01:44.059
2. Your contracts checklist and your risk register.

16
00:01:44.059 --> 00:01:50.363
3. Your calendar: every deadline and frequency, each with an owner.

17
00:01:50.763 --> 00:01:51.363
What to avoid

18
00:01:51.363 --> 00:01:55.926
Asking legal questions after launch instead of before.

19
00:01:55.926 --> 00:02:01.230
Treating unconfirmed items as settled: mark what has been checked.

20
00:02:01.230 --> 00:02:07.904
Mapping only one country when you plan to work in several.

21
00:02:08.504 --> 00:02:10.304
You build your legal map and a list of open legal questions.

22
00:02:10.304 --> 00:02:14.304
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

23
00:02:15.804 --> 00:02:18.904
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
